## Supabase Database Management

Supabase provides a PostgreSQL database with additional features like real-time subscriptions, authentication, and storage. It's an excellent choice for Next.js applications requiring a managed database solution.

### Supabase CLI Setup and Usage

**Installation and Authentication**:
```bash
# Install Supabase CLI globally
npm i -g supabase

# Login to Supabase
supabase login

# Link project to Supabase
supabase link --project-ref your-project-ref
```

**Local Development**:
```bash
# Start local Supabase instance
supabase start

# Stop local Supabase instance
supabase stop

# Reset local database
supabase db reset

# View local services status
supabase status
```

**Database Schema Management**:
```bash
# Pull remote database schema
supabase db pull

# Push local migrations to remote
supabase db push

# Create a new migration
supabase migration new migration_name

# View database diff
supabase db diff

# View database diff with specific schema
supabase db diff --schema public
```

**Type Generation**:
```bash
# Generate TypeScript types from database
supabase gen types typescript --local > types/supabase.ts

# Generate types from remote database
supabase gen types typescript --project-id your-project-ref > types/supabase.ts

# Generate types for specific schema
supabase gen types typescript --local --schema public > types/supabase.ts
```

**Database Operations**:
```bash
# Execute SQL file
supabase db execute --file migration.sql

# Open database in browser (local)
supabase db open

# View database logs
supabase db logs

# Backup database
supabase db dump -f backup.sql

# Restore database from backup
supabase db restore backup.sql
```

### Supabase Migration Workflow

**Development Workflow**:
```bash
# 1. Create migration from schema changes
supabase migration new add_user_table

# 2. Edit migration file in supabase/migrations/

# 3. Apply migration locally
supabase db reset

# 4. Test migration
supabase db test

# 5. Push to remote
supabase db push
```

**Production Migration Workflow**:
```bash
# 1. Review migrations
supabase migration list

# 2. Test migrations on staging
supabase db push --db-url $STAGING_DATABASE_URL

# 3. Apply to production
supabase db push --db-url $PRODUCTION_DATABASE_URL

# 4. Verify migration
